A character turnaround reference sheet populated by exactly one figure, the same single elderly male mouse, repeated in three full-body drawings arranged in one centered horizontal row with clear gaps between them: front view, then side view, then back view. Each figure sits entirely within its own margin, wholly clear of every edge of the image. A seamless plain warm apricot-toned paper backdrop, the same paper as the rest of this production, fills the entire background in a flat, even, colour-neutral wash of light, uniform and shadowless across the whole sheet. All three figures are exactly the same height and build, standing upright in a neutral relaxed pose, drawn small enough that each complete body fits inside the frame with empty space above every head and a clear strip of perfectly clean bare paper below every pair of feet; feet are fully visible, resting well above the bottom edge. He is an old grey field mouse, broad-shouldered and heavy-set, with a long scar across his left brow and one notched ear, coarse grey fur and white whiskers, a pink weathered nose. He wears a patched green wool cloak with the hood down over a dented brass breastplate and a cream linen shirt with a brown leather belt; the scar and notched ear are present and identical in the front view, the side view and the back view. Illustrated storybook realism on warm apricot-toned paper, visible paper grain and fibre, ink linework with watercolour and gouache washes, fur drawn as strokes never photographic.
A character turnaround reference sheet populated by exactly one figure, the same single female dormouse, repeated in three full-body drawings arranged in one centered horizontal row with clear gaps between them: front view, then side view, then back view. Each figure sits entirely within its own margin, wholly clear of every edge of the image. A seamless plain warm apricot-toned paper backdrop, the same paper as the rest of this production, fills the entire background in a flat, even, colour-neutral wash of light, uniform and shadowless across the whole sheet. All three figures are exactly the same height and build, standing upright in a neutral relaxed pose, drawn small enough that each complete body fits inside the frame with empty space above every head and a clear strip of perfectly clean bare paper below every pair of feet; feet are fully visible, resting well above the bottom edge. She is a small stout dormouse, round-faced with bright dark eyes and a flour smudge on one cheek, warm russet fur and a bun of whiskers tied with twine, a pink nose and paws faintly stained with berry juice. She wears rolled cream linen sleeves under a long ochre apron over a brown dress, with wooden clogs; the apron and the berry-stained paws are present and identical in the front view, the side view and the back view. Illustrated storybook realism on warm apricot-toned paper, visible paper grain and fibre, ink linework with watercolour and gouache washes, fur drawn as strokes never photographic.
A character turnaround reference sheet populated by exactly one figure, the same single young adult male rat, repeated in three full-body drawings arranged in one centered horizontal row with clear gaps between them: front view, then side view, then back view. Each figure sits entirely within its own margin, wholly clear of every edge of the image. A seamless plain warm apricot-toned paper backdrop, the same paper as the rest of this production, fills the entire background in a flat, even, colour-neutral wash of light, uniform and shadowless across the whole sheet. All three figures are exactly the same height and build, standing upright in a neutral relaxed pose, drawn small enough that each complete body fits inside the frame with empty space above every head and a clear strip of perfectly clean bare paper below every pair of feet; feet are fully visible, resting well above the bottom edge. He is a lean black rat, tall and rangy, with a narrow muzzle and a pale burn-mark down the right side of his jaw, sleek black fur, a grey nose, scarred paws, and bare feet. He wears a long oilskin travelling coat the colour of wet slate with no armour beneath it; the burn-mark and the slate oilskin coat are present and identical in the front view, the side view and the back view. Illustrated storybook realism on warm apricot-toned paper, visible paper grain and fibre, ink linework with watercolour and gouache washes, fur drawn as strokes never photographic.
A survey photograph reference plate, the space empty of any figure or person, a sandstone gatehouse arch with two iron-banded oak doors, one ajar, a flagged yard beyond, a lantern bracket to the left of the arch, wet sandstone blocks with moss in the joints, dusk light in light rain, one lit lantern, the sky slate-blue, a few orange wildflowers at the wall foot on otherwise bare ground. Lit exactly as this production is lit, not for legibility. Illustrated storybook realism on warm apricot-toned paper, visible paper grain and fibre, ink linework with watercolour and gouache washes, fur drawn as strokes never photographic.
A survey photograph reference plate, the space empty of any figure or person, the great kitchen of a sandstone abbey: a wide stone hearth under an oak beam with a low fire lit, a long scrubbed oak table, a low stool, a stone-flagged floor, copper pans hanging on hooks, flour dust on the table, one lit candle, warm amber light, shadows pooling under the table, the floor otherwise bare. Lit exactly as this production is lit, not for legibility. Illustrated storybook realism on warm apricot-toned paper, visible paper grain and fibre, ink linework with watercolour and gouache washes, fur drawn as strokes never photographic.
A survey photograph reference plate, the space empty of any figure or person, a wide view of a sandstone abbey on a green hill above autumn woods at evening, a river catching the last light in the valley below, two chimneys with smoke rising, red-tiled roofs, a handful of lantern-lit windows, a single empty cart track, russet and ochre canopy. Lit exactly as this production is lit, not for legibility. Illustrated storybook realism on warm apricot-toned paper, visible paper grain and fibre, ink linework with watercolour and gouache washes, fur drawn as strokes never photographic.
